      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\(x^2+\frac{8}{3}x+\frac{14}{9}=0\)</para>
          <para>Find the exact solutions by completing the square.</para>
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\frac{14}{9} &amp;=&amp;0 \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\left(\frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{8}{3}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9}+\left(\frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{8}{3}\right)^{2} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9}+\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\frac{16}{9} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9}+\frac{16}{9} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\frac{16}{9} &amp;=&amp;\frac{2}{9} \\ \left(x+\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;\frac{2}{9} \\ \sqrt{\left(x+\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2}} &amp;=&amp;\sqrt{\frac{2}{9}} \\ x+\frac{4}{3} &amp;=&amp;\pm \frac{\sqrt{2}}{3} \\ x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{4}{3} \pm \frac{\sqrt{2}}{3} \end{array}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
