      <section>
        <title>Are you ready for more?</title>
        <exercise class="RFM1">
          <problem>
            <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
            <para>What quadratic equation of the form \(ax^2+bx+c=0\) would have the solutions \(x=5− \sqrt{2}\) and \(x=5+ \sqrt{2}\)?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Enter the quadratic equation.</para>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>\(x^2−10x+23=0\). Working backward, these are solutions to \((x−5)^2=2\). In standard form, this is \(x^2−10x+23=0\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
